{"meta": {"limit": 500, "next": null, "offset": 0, "previous": null, "total_count": 9}, "objects": [{"abstract": "   The Robots Exclusion Protocol defined in [RFC9309] specifies the\n   user-agent rule for targeting automatic clients either by prefix\n   matching their self-defined product token or by a global rule * that\n   matches all clients.\n\n   This document extends [RFC9309] by defining a new rule for targeting\n   automatic clients based on the clients' purpose for accessing the\n   service.\n", "ad": null, "expires": "2025-04-21T11:38:10Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/2440/", "id": 139804, "intended_std_level": null, "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-illyes-rep-purpose", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 4, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-illyes-rep-purpose/", "rev": "00", "rfc": null, "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": null, "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/2/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/", "/api/v1/doc/state/134/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "submissions": ["/api/v1/submit/submission/146545/"], "tags": [], "time": "2025-04-21T07:05:16Z", "title": "Robots Exclusion Protocol User Agent Purpose Extension", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   This document proposes a vocabulary for expressing content\n   preferences for rightsholders who wish to manage the use of their\n   content in AI training.  This vocabulary allows publishers to express\n   preferences through metadata or content-delivery protocols.  The\n   vocabulary can be applied at different levels of granularity and\n   incorporates preferences for permissions, usage scope, and data\n   retention, providing a foundation for interoperability across various\n   Internet protocols.\n", "ad": null, "expires": "2025-07-24T12:37:34Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/2440/", "id": 142662, "intended_std_level": null, "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-vaughan-aipref-vocab", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 13, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-vaughan-aipref-vocab/", "rev": "00", "rfc": null, "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": null, "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/2/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/", "/api/v1/doc/state/134/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "submissions": ["/api/v1/submit/submission/148596/"], "tags": [], "time": "2025-07-24T07:09:02Z", "title": "Vocabulary for Expressing Content Preferences for AI Training", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   This document proposes a standardized vocabulary of use cases that\n   can be targeted when expressing machine-readable opt-outs related to\n   Text and Data Mining (TDM) and AI training.  The vocabulary is\n   agnostic to specific opt-out mechanisms and enables declaring parties\n   to communicate restrictions or permissions regarding the use of their\n   digital assets in a structured and interoperable manner.  It defines\n   three key use cases—TDM, AI Training, and Generative AI\n   Training—which can be referenced by opt-out systems to ensure\n   consistent interpretation across different implementations.\n", "ad": null, "expires": "2025-10-01T09:12:25Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/2440/", "id": 145272, "intended_std_level": null, "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-keller-aipref-vocab", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 6, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-keller-aipref-vocab/", "rev": "01", "rfc": null, "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": null, "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/4/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/", "/api/v1/doc/state/35/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "submissions": ["/api/v1/submit/submission/150867/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/150828/"], "tags": [], "time": "2025-04-10T14:46:31Z", "title": "Proposal for an Opt-Out Vocabulary", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   Content creators and other stakeholders might wish to signal their\n   preferences about how their content might be consumed by automated\n   systems.  This document defines how preferences can be signaled as\n   part of the acquisition of content in HTTP.\n\n   This document updates RFC 9309 to allow for the inclusion of usage\n   preferences.\n", "ad": null, "expires": "2025-11-29T01:55:19Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/2440/", "id": 146261, "intended_std_level": null, "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-it-aipref-attachment", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 7, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-it-aipref-attachment/", "rev": "00", "rfc": null, "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": null, "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/4/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/", "/api/v1/doc/state/35/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "submissions": ["/api/v1/submit/submission/152344/"], "tags": [], "time": "2025-05-28T02:45:54Z", "title": "Indicating Preferences Regarding Content Usage", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   Content creators and other stakeholders might wish to signal their\n   preferences about how their content might be consumed by automated\n   systems.  This document defines a very simple format for expressions.\n\n   This document updates RFC 9309 to define one means of conveyance.  An\n   HTTP header field is also defined.\n", "ad": null, "expires": "2025-08-21T04:48:33Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/2440/", "id": 143072, "intended_std_level": null, "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-thomson-aipref-sup", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 17, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-thomson-aipref-sup/", "rev": "00", "rfc": null, "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": null, "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/2/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/", "/api/v1/doc/state/134/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "submissions": ["/api/v1/submit/submission/149230/"], "tags": [], "time": "2025-08-20T07:09:01Z", "title": "Short Usage Preference Strings for Automated Processing", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   This document defines a vocabulary for expressing preferences\n   regarding how digital assets are used by automated processing\n   systems.  This vocabulary allows for the declaration of restrictions\n   or permissions for use of digital assets by such systems.\n", "ad": null, "expires": "2027-03-18T06:18:02Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/2440/", "id": 145883, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/ps/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-aipref-vocab", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 15, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-aipref-vocab/", "rev": "08", "rfc": null, "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": null, "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/", "/api/v1/doc/state/38/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "submissions": ["/api/v1/submit/submission/151698/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/152854/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/154124/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/155077/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/157033/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/157845/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/162670/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/167868/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/169000/"], "tags": [], "time": "2026-09-14T06:18:02Z", "title": "A Vocabulary For Expressing AI Usage Preferences", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   Methods are defined for associating usage preferences with content\n   that is obtained using the HTTP protocol.  This document defines\n   attachment methods using the Robots Exclusion Protocol and HTTP\n   header fields.\n\n   This document updates RFC 9309 to allow for the inclusion of usage\n   preferences.\n", "ad": null, "expires": "2027-02-20T04:25:16Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/2440/", "id": 146479, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/ps/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-aipref-attach", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 10, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-aipref-attach/", "rev": "05", "rfc": null, "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": null, "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/", "/api/v1/doc/state/38/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "submissions": ["/api/v1/submit/submission/152771/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/152853/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/154123/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/155076/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/157032/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/167869/"], "tags": [], "time": "2026-08-19T04:25:16Z", "title": "Associating AI Usage Preferences with Content in HTTP", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   This Internet Draft proposes a category entitled \"AI Substitutive\n   Use\" which would enable parties to express a preference regarding how\n   digital assets are used by automated processing systems, with a focus\n   on post-training (inference-time) uses that are likely to result in\n   the creation of AI-generated outputs that substitute for the original\n   asset.  The proposal is for this category to nest within the larger\n   category of Automated Processing, currently envisaged in the working\n   group draft [AIPREF-VOCAB] (21 July 2025).\n", "ad": null, "expires": "2026-03-12T21:05:18Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/2440/", "id": 149492, "intended_std_level": null, "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-silver-aipref-vocab-substitutive", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 5, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-silver-aipref-vocab-substitutive/", "rev": "00", "rfc": null, "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": null, "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/2/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/", "/api/v1/doc/state/134/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "submissions": ["/api/v1/submit/submission/155139/"], "tags": [], "time": "2026-03-16T07:09:26Z", "title": "Vocabulary For Expressing AI Substitutive Usage", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   This document proposes a standardized vocabulary to express\n   preferences for usage of digital content collected by Search and AI\n   crawlers.  This vocabulary allows for the creation of structured\n   declarations about restrictions or permissions for use of content\n   retrieved by such systems.  Adding the No updates on March 24, 2026\n   to keep document from expiring.\n", "ad": null, "expires": "2026-09-26T23:25:27Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/2440/", "id": 149645, "intended_std_level": null, "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-madhavan-aipref-displaybasedpref", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 10, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-madhavan-aipref-displaybasedpref/", "rev": "02", "rfc": null, "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": null, "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/2/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/", "/api/v1/doc/state/134/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "submissions": ["/api/v1/submit/submission/155407/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/155417/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/161617/"], "tags": [], "time": "2026-09-26T07:09:02Z", "title": "A Vocabulary for Controlling Usage of Content Collected by Search and AI Crawlers", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}]}